{# ============================================================================
   THE RAIL BESIDE THE REPORT FORM.

   The form is 860px wide and the screen is not, so on a wide viewport there was a
   column of nothing beside a form somebody was filling in. What belongs there is
   the two things the form cannot say for itself:

     THE OBSERVATION, IN FULL — only where the filing came from a record. The strip
     at the top of the page proves it exists; this makes it legible.

     WHAT THIS KIND ASKS — always. Every block the chosen sub-category switched on,
     with the gate's own marks against them.

   A WALK-IN FILING IS THE SECOND CARD ALONE, and that is the commonest filing
   there is: somebody walked into an office, there is no record behind it, and the
   rail is still the place that says what is left to answer.

   ONE SCROLLER. The rail is not a scroll region of its own — the page is the
   scroller, so there is one scrollbar to find and nothing in the rail can be
   stranded beside a form that has grown long. Below 1160px the two columns cannot
   both stand and the rail stacks under the form, which keeps its width: the rail is
   extra help, never a reason for the form to get narrower (see incidents.css).

   Parameters: controller, kinds, chosen, prefill, checklists, sourceFiles, sourceMap
   ========================================================================== #}
<aside class="i-rail">
    {% if prefill.hasProvenance %}
        {{ include('@UhifadhiIncident/report/_observation.html.twig', {
            prefill: prefill,
            files: sourceFiles,
            map: sourceMap,
        }, with_context: false) }}
    {% endif %}

    {{ include('@UhifadhiIncident/report/_checklist.html.twig', {
        controller: controller,
        kinds: kinds,
        chosen: chosen,
        prefill: prefill,
        checklists: checklists,
    }, with_context: false) }}
</aside>
